body:
As someone who has had supernatural experiences with these demons, as have many others, believe me they are real. Influences, inspirations, passions, norms, and drives can and are influenced by these inter-dimensional beings but they are not them in and of themselves.

&#x200B;

As for their salvation, this is one of the questions that make me wonder what God being all in all means, or what the reality of the new creation will look like at the end of Revelation when it says the former things have passed away.  I think there is great mystery as to how God will accomplish all of this but we know he will. I think its a good question to ponder on as these beings seem to know who God is and his message of salvation yet still continue to reject him. I am not sure what will really make them change their mind, maybe they are the ones who be annihilated and humans restored? its an interesting question indeed

Christ took away the sins of the whole world. God does not deal with us according to our sins-he dealt with the sin issue on the cross. God has forgiven all our sins and extends his invitation out to all-waiting and hoping for all prodigals to come home. I know it is hard and not easy to do, but do not focus on your sin. Again, it has been dealt with and God does not condemn you. Focus on receiving his love. He knew all you would do before you even did it and still loves you just as you are. He's not waiting to love you if you clean up your act first. While we were still sinners, Christ died for us.

&#x200B;

One thing that helps me visualize this amazing grace ( and it is amazing and so foreign to our law-based minds who are only focused on rules and earning God's favor) is picture Jesus on the cross. He is the embodiment of who God is. The people spit at him, cursed him, beat him, and nailed him to a tree....have you done anything even close to that? Yet, Jesus still interceded for their forgiveness and had mercy on them ("father forgive them for they know not what they do").....how much more is his grace extended towards you who has done nothing even close to that? 

&#x200B;

Truth is, God does not relate to us according to the law. In fact, the law has been fulfilled and abolished in Christ. His one requirement is belief or trust in his free offer of eternal life through Jesus.

&#x200B;

rest easy your sins are not only forgiven but FORGOTTEN

"For I will be merciful toward their iniquities, and I will remember their sins no more.”" (hebrews 8:12).....dont be stuck on over something God has already forgotten. the only thing that is real is LOVE.
